  "answer": "Tooth decay starts when the pH of the mouth is lower than 5.5 because tooth enamel, which is made of calcium phosphate, begins to corrode under acidic conditions. The pH of the mouth drops below 5.5 due to the production of acids by bacteria that break down sugar and food particles in the mouth. These acids lower the pH, leading to the dissolution of tooth enamel and the onset of tooth decay. To prevent this, it is important to clean the mouth after eating and use toothpaste that is basic to neutralize the excess acid.",
